---
permalink: /sitemap.xml
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
{%- comment -%}
On .org this is a sitemap INDEX pointing at one child per bucket (see
src/_data/sitemapBuckets.js for why). robots.txt still advertises this one URL, and
submitting it to GSC/Bing pulls the children in automatically — but coverage is
then reported per child, which is the whole point.

On .com sitemapBuckets is empty and this stays a flat sitemap: four URLs do not
need an index, and empty children are a GSC error.
{%- endcomment -%}
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
{%- if sitemapBuckets.size > 0 -%}
<sitemapindex xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
{%- for b in sitemapBuckets %}
  <sitemap>
    <loc>{{ siteUrl }}/sitemap-{{ b.name }}.xml</loc>
  </sitemap>
{%- endfor %}
</sitemapindex>
{%- else -%}
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
{%- include "sitemap-urls.html", bucket: "all" -%}
</urlset>
{%- endif -%}
